@article{merged1089,
 abstract = {Generative artificial intelligence (GAI) has brought significant impacts
on teaching modes, learning methods, educational concepts, educational
resource organization, and talent cultivation. Existing research mainly
explores the impact of GAI on education from the perspective of
educational technology or pedagogy. However, the influence of GAI on
individual teachers, teams, and overall school organizations should not
be underestimated, it's necessary to analyze the impact of GAI on
education from the perspective of organizational behavior. Research has
shown that at the individual level of teachers, the penetration of GAI
has a dual impact on their work pressure, further enhancing the moral
intensity of education and raising higher requirements for teachers'
ethical sensitivity. Collaborative decision-making between humans and
machines will help achieve ``intelligent enhancement{''}; At the team
level, the human-machine hybrid teaching team will showcase the new
productivity of the school. Human machine trust helps to build a
human-machine hybrid team, and mutually beneficial human-machine
symbiotic relationships become the goal of building a human-machine
hybrid team. In the operation of the team, GAI provides more
possibilities for team conflict management; At the organizational level,
the school's organizational structure will face restructuring, and the
work content, responsibilities, and processes of teachers and managers
will be redesigned. School policies and organizational culture will also
be re-examined and adjusted.},
