@article{merged1162,
 abstract = {Continued efforts to incorporate the use of artificial intelligence
within post-secondary education efforts requires its incorporation by
teachers in their day-to-day educational practices. Generative
artificial intelligence, through platforms like ChatGPT, introduce
opportunities and cautions to its' use with teaching-learning, but it is
equally important to consider a more comprehensive picture of artificial
intelligence's (AI) use within education. The merits of using AI in
teaching practices to support student learning may be undervalued by
teachers and therefore under utilised. A paucity of available tools to
explore teachers' intentions to use AI is a pressing issue. The creation
and testing for reliability and validity of one tool, the Artificial
Intelligence Acceptance Measurement Survey (AIAMS) is discussed in this
article. It is believed that the AIAMS will serve to support further
research and understanding of what influences teachers and their
intentions to use AI within their teaching efforts. The important role
teachers realise with student learning suggests that research focused on
this area is imperative as we move forward in working with AI in
education.},
