 abstract = {This paper reflects on how we, as instructors of Introduction to Human
Geography, navigated the widespread usage of Generative Artificial
Intelligence (GAI) models in the classroom. We discuss how GAI first
appeared in our classroom, how we connect GAI to course content in
lecture periods, and present reflections on navigating GAI in course
writing assignments. Our conclusion advocates for a holistic framework
which addresses GAI usage to not police the boundaries of what is or is
not ``good work{''} but rather encourage students to develop skills,
techniques, and creative engagement with course concepts that transfer
beyond the classroom and workplace.},
