@article{merged1307,
 abstract = {The main objective of this study is to focus on the actual impact and
current status of Generative Artificial Intelligence (Gen AI) on art and
design curriculum education in higher education. The text revolves
around the relationship between aesthetic education, interdisciplinary
education and AI in art and design course education, and we try to
answer the following questions: Can traditional aesthetic education for
art and design creation be discarded with the help of Gen AI? Is
interdisciplinary course teaching simplified with the help of AI? What
role should AI play as a digital creation platform in art and design
education? In this paper, through an in-depth analysis of Gen AI in art
and design teaching experiments, we explore in detail its practical
application in the process of university art and design teaching
practices and how it affects traditional teaching practices, curriculum
design and student-teacher interactions.},
