@article{merged1769,
 abstract = {Generative Artificial Intelligence is occupying all spheres of our daily
lives: work, economics, culture, education, politics, and the key lies
in harnessing its potential to our advantage. It is a phenomenon that
poses new and complex challenges for higher education, especially the
teaching role if we take into account the training of the professionals
of the future. Open AI's chatbot, known worldwide as Chat GPT, still has
a record 3.5 million users on its first day of ``life{''}. A year after
its release, young people are using it every day at university, and we
are curious to know how and what for. This is a moment in which the
university should be oriented towards the production of sovereign and
critical knowledge mediated by AI. What potential is there in the
intersection between education and work from generative AI and why is
its development and promotion essential? What competences and skills
become crucial? And most of all, what students are we educating?
Concerns that arise from the field of Communication in Argentina, taking
as a case study a research project that is being carried out with
Communication undergraduates and related careers.},
